<zk>
	<label multiline="true">
		ZK-6112 Marble defaults from zk.xml. Use the buttons to set a library property and reload:
		1. "compact": the html element gets data-density="compact" and the textbox is shorter.
		2. "slate": the html element gets data-brand="slate" and the button turns slate grey.
		3. "#0a7d5a": the button turns green with no flash of the default blue on reload.
		4. Then click "apply copper": the button turns copper (runtime switch beats the zk.xml default).
		5. "reset": back to the default blue, comfortable page.
	</label>
	<hlayout>
		<button label="compact" onClick='org.zkoss.lang.Library.setProperty("org.zkoss.theme.marble.density", "compact");Executions.sendRedirect(null);'/>
		<button label="slate" onClick='org.zkoss.lang.Library.setProperty("org.zkoss.theme.marble.brand", "slate");Executions.sendRedirect(null);'/>
		<button label="#0a7d5a" onClick='org.zkoss.lang.Library.setProperty("org.zkoss.theme.marble.brand", "#0a7d5a");Executions.sendRedirect(null);'/>
		<button label="reset" onClick='org.zkoss.lang.Library.setProperty("org.zkoss.theme.marble.density", null);org.zkoss.lang.Library.setProperty("org.zkoss.theme.marble.brand", null);Executions.sendRedirect(null);'/>
	</hlayout>
	<hlayout>
		<textbox value="textbox"/>
		<button id="copper" label="apply copper" onClick="org.zkoss.zul.theme.MarbleBrand.apply(org.zkoss.zul.theme.MarbleBrand.Brand.COPPER)"/>
	</hlayout>
</zk>
